Rebased copy of Vincent Guittot's [PATCH 00/18 v2] 'Improving latency of short slice tasks'.
Upstream: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-pm/20261002154415.2270586-1-vincent.guittot@linaro.org/
(the full upstream 18-patch mbox is kept alongside as ..._short_slice_tasks.patch, unreferenced)

Rebased 2026-10-04 onto torvalds master 6addb4f3 (7.3.0-rc5) with pongoKernel's patch stack applied.
Method: per-file three-way merge (git merge-file), base = tip/sched/core at 53bc5c556,
which is the queue state the series was written against (it applies there with fuzz 0, 0 failures).

One conflict, in enqueue_task_fair(): the series' base assumes the queued commit
'sched/fair: Remove dead code on enqueue_task_fair()', which this tree does not have.
Resolution keeps this tree's curr/place_entity block and adds the series'
decay_entity_lag() call above it. Everything else merged cleanly.

